---@field tab_id? string|distilled.Null Opaque per-browser-tab id (see the frontend `getTabId`). On an async request it ref-counts this tab as a consumer of the shared chart-data task so a cancel/navigate-away from one tab doesn't abort a task another tab still awaits. Read by the API as a request-level routing hint; not part of the query context.

