---@class apache_superset.ImportAssetRequest
---@field bundle? string upload file (ZIP or JSON)
---@field encrypted_extra_secrets? string JSON map of secret values for masked encrypted_extra fields. Each key is a database file path and the value is a map of JSONPath expressions to secret values. For example: `{"databases/db.yaml": {"$.credentials_info.secret": "foo"}}`.
---@field overwrite? boolean overwrite existing assets? Defaults to ``true`` for backwards compatibility. When ``false``, the import fails if any of the assets already exist.
---@field passwords? string|distilled.Secret JSON map of passwords for each featured database in the ZIP file. If the ZIP includes a database config in the path `databases/MyDatabase.yaml`, the password should be provided in the following format: `{"databases/MyDatabase.yaml": "my_password"}`.
---@field sparse? boolean allow sparse update of resources
---@field ssh_tunnel_passwords? string|distilled.Secret JSON map of passwords for each ssh_tunnel associated to a featured database in the ZIP file. If the ZIP includes a ssh_tunnel config in the path `databases/MyDatabase.yaml`, the password should be provided in the following format: `{"databases/MyDatabase.yaml": "my_password"}`.
---@field ssh_tunnel_private_key_passwords? string|distilled.Secret JSON map of private_key_passwords for each ssh_tunnel associated to a featured database in the ZIP file. If the ZIP includes a ssh_tunnel config in the path `databases/MyDatabase.yaml`, the private_key should be provided in the following format: `{"databases/MyDatabase.yaml": "my_private_key_password"}`.
---@field ssh_tunnel_private_keys? string JSON map of private_keys for each ssh_tunnel associated to a featured database in the ZIP file. If the ZIP includes a ssh_tunnel config in the path `databases/MyDatabase.yaml`, the private_key should be provided in the following format: `{"databases/MyDatabase.yaml": "my_private_key"}`.

