---@field include_cta? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to include the call-to-action link back to Superset (e.g. 'Explore in Superset') in the delivered notifications
---@field log_retention? number How long to keep the logs around for this report (in days)
---@field name? string The report schedule name.
---@field recipients? apache_superset.PutReportRequestRecipientsList
---@field report_format? apache_superset.PutReportRequestReportFormat|string Attachment format. NONE disables attachments for alerts and makes chart/dashboard optional. Omitted attachment settings are preserved on update.
---@field retry_max_attempts? number Maximum number of retry attempts (1–10)
---@field retry_notify_owners? boolean Notify report owners on each retry attempt
---@field retry_notify_recipients? boolean Notify report recipients on each retry attempt
---@field retry_on_failure? boolean Enable automatic retries on report failure
---@field run_alert_query_as? number|distilled.Null ID of the user whose credentials are used when running the alert condition SQL query, useful when the audience of the alert does not have access to the database. Null inherits the content executor at execution time.
---@field run_alert_query_as_type? apache_superset.PutReportRequestRunAlertQueryAsType|string|distilled.Null Alert query executor type; null inherits run_as.
---@field run_as? number|distilled.Null ID of the user whose credentials (RBAC permissions, database OAuth2 tokens) are used when rendering the content (screenshot, PDF, CSV, XLSX or text). Admins can set any active user; non-admins can only set themselves. Onlyhonored when the ALERT_REPORT_DYNAMIC_EXECUTOR feature flag is enabled. Admins can set this and run_as_type to null to use ALERT_REPORTS_EXECUTORS.
---@field run_as_type? apache_superset.PutReportRequestRunAsType|string|distilled.Null Explicit executor type; fixed_user requires run_as.
---@field send_failed_reports? boolean Send the failed report to all recipients after retries are exhausted
---@field sql? string|distilled.Null A SQL statement that defines whether the alert should get triggered or not. The query is expected to return either NULL or a number value.
---@field timezone? apache_superset.PutReportRequestTimezone|string A timezone string that represents the location of the timezone.
---@field type? apache_superset.PutReportRequestType|string The report schedule type
---@field validator_config_json? apache_superset.ValidatorConfigJSON
---@field validator_type? apache_superset.PutReportRequestValidatorType|string|distilled.Null Determines when to trigger alert based off value from alert query. Alerts will be triggered with these validator types: - Not Null - When the return value is Not NULL, Empty, or 0 - Operator - When `sql_return_value comparison_operator threshold` is True e.g. `50 <= 75`<br>Supports the comparison operators <, <=, >, >=, ==, and !=
---@field working_timeout? number|distilled.Null If an alert is staled at a working state, how long until it's state is reset to error

